---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Open a bank account in Andorra | Andbank, MoraBanc, Creand"
  description="How to open a bank account in Andorra: KYC, no online onboarding, identity and source of funds. The three groups are Andbank, MoraBanc and Creand."
  path="/opening-a-bank-account"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Open a bank account in Andorra</h1>
    <p>
      To open a bank account in Andorra you go through Andbank, MoraBanc
      or Creand. The Association of Andorran Banks treats it as a
      compliance process, not a form from hotel Wi-Fi.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Taken from
        <a
          href="https://www.andorranbanking.ad/en/footer-links/faq/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Andorran Banking’s FAQ</a
        >
        and the
        <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AFA</a>.
        The association notes that non-resident accounts may carry a
        minimum value because of the cost of checking foreign funds. Each
        bank sets its own threshold. We do not invent those numbers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Who may apply</h2>
    <p>
      Andorran Banking states that any natural or legal person may apply
      to open an account, and that banks may refuse a customer if they
      suspect illicit funds. Companies, whether domiciled in Andorra or
      abroad, may also apply. The association lists constitution
      documents, tax identification, powers and evidence of activity
      among the papers banks typically ask for.
    </p>

    <h2>What the banks say they will ask</h2>
    <p>
      Accounts cannot be opened directly on the internet. KYC requires
      the bank to identify the customer properly. The FAQ describes a
      meeting with a banker, an official photo identity document, and
      evidence of the origin of funds: a purchase contract, a reference
      from a foreign bank, or other papers the bank requires. There are
      no anonymous accounts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Andorra applies international tax-information standards. Andorran
      Banking publishes notes on automatic exchange of information. New
      accounts involve a tax-residence self-certification. Discretion in
      private banking is not a shield for a criminal or tax
      investigation.
    </p>

    <h2>Supervision</h2>
    <p>
      The same FAQ states that Andorran banking is supervised by the
      <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Andorran Financial Authority</a
      >,
      which has supervisory, control and disciplinary powers over the
      financial system.
    </p>

    <h2>The three groups</h2>
    <p>
      Andorran Banking currently presents three banking groups. We list
      each from its own site:
    </p>
    <div class="official-links">
      <a href="/directory/andbank">Andbank</a>
      <a href="/directory/morabanc">MoraBanc</a>
      <a href="/directory/creand">Creand (Crèdit Andorrà)</a>
    </div>
    <p>
      Often, a residence file and an account are prepared together. See
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      and
      <a href="/directory">the directory</a>
      for counsel. Buying property is
      <a href="/buying-property">a separate note</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you will need an introduction to Andorran banking or counsel."
    source="opening-a-bank-account"
  />
</Base>
